  "interpretation": "In TCGA-LUAD most tumors are coded NOS/Mixed (310/507), and aggressive subtypes solid/micropapillary are rare (5/3) so the hypothesis 'solid physiotype-3-bad-prognosis' cannot be tested with enough power. Weak overall association physiotype x histology (chi2 p=0.048, Cramer's V=0.17); a histology-only classifier does not beat the majority baseline (0.647 vs 0.645), so histology cannot substitute RNA-based physiotyping. Relative to NOS, the large subtypes trend to better OS: Papillary HR=0.48 (p=0.048), Acinar HR=0.42 (p=0.053), Mixed HR=0.73 (p=0.073); median OS is lowest for NOS (1229 d) vs Mixed 1725 d and Papillary 2681 d."
